we have new information about the final  moments before a plane crashed near  Dallas killing everyone on board the  names of seven of the ten victims have  been revealed you'll recall this small  plane dove into a hangar shortly after  takeoff on Sunday Kris Van Cleave is  tracking the investigation  Kris good morning what has the NTSB  found so far  well good morning we also have some new  pictures to show you take a look at this  this is the roof of the hangar you can  see where the plane tore through now the  aircraft does not have a flight data  recorder but right now investigators are  poring over the planes cockpit voice  recorder listening not only to the  conversation on board but for background  noises that could be clues about what  went so terribly wrong the pilots were  cleared for takeoff they acknowledged  takeoff the National Transportation  Safety Board released new images from  its investigation after a twin engine  Beechcraft King Air crashed into a  hangar shortly after takeoff killing all  10 aboard Sunday north of Dallas among  the wreckage the NTSB found the cockpit  voice recorder of particular interest to  us is the internal cockpit conversation  between the pilot and the copilot there  is little left of the plane but  investigators do know the landing gear  was still down when the plane struck the  hangar the NTSB does have radar  information and video of the crash  he just banked over rolled over and came  straight down into the building as well  as witness accounts pilot David Snell  saw the crash from a nearby hangar when  you see an airplane turn on its side low  to the ground you're not gonna recover  from that I mean it was just horrible  among those killed 15 year-old Alice  Merritt Otto and her 13 year old brother  Dylan they were traveling with their  mother Ornella  and stepfather Brian Ehlert the couple  owned a restaurant in Dallas 27 year old  Matthew Palmer was one of the pilots he  had recently celebrated his one-year  wedding anniversary Steven Leath Allen  and his wife Gina were also onboard all  my years of flying I've never seen  anything like that but my thoughts are  for the families that people the lives  changed and there's nothing you can do  about it  Textron aviation the manufacture of  Beechcraft planes is cooperating with  the NTSB investigation it can take this  keyboard a year or more in cases like  this to determine the probable cause of  the crash Tony
 

